>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. W–N–O 170.27°, N–O 1.20353 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.4942. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +2 and total charge +0. The published crystal structure locates both the nitrosyl and ancillary ligands; Formal net charges on the ancillary ligands were also checked against the same-ID tmQMg-L record. The coordination environment, original bond angle, lengths and bond orders support the NO⁺ limiting form. Localized 5 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 52 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 48 nonmetal covalent bonds: 46 within range, 1 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 32–34 C-C 1.4074 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

