>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Mo–N–O 168.86°, N–O 1.20165 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.5082. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +2 and total charge +0. Terminal ligand identity, the remaining graph and charge balance were checked; The original M–N–O angle, M–N and N–O distances, and WBO agree with documented NO⁺ controls matched by metal, formal state, NO count and ligand class. Localized 5 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 58 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 54 nonmetal covalent bonds: 52 within range, 1 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 3–4 C-O 1.1959 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

